# TOOLS.md

Local-system facts the bot needs but that don't belong in `MEMORY.md`. Add as you go; keep entries short.

## Static ffmpeg
Path: `/home/node/.openclaw/.bin/ffmpeg` (mounted from host `/root/.openclaw/.bin/ffmpeg`). Survives image upgrades. Don't use the system ffmpeg — it may be missing or broken inside the container.

## Chromium remote debugging (only if your bot uses a browser)
Inside container, connect to the host's Chrome via **`172.17.0.1:9222`** (Docker bridge). Don't use `localhost`.

```js
const ws = (await (await fetch('http://172.17.0.1:9222/json/version')).json()).webSocketDebuggerUrl;
const browser = await puppeteer.connect({ browserWSEndpoint: ws });
```

Always `page.close()` when done.

## Media file delivery (Telegram)
Save generated media (audio, images, video) to `/home/node/.openclaw/workspace/generated/`, **not** `/tmp/`. Send via `MEDIA:./generated/filename.ext`.

## Reply language
The user prefers **{{LANGUAGE}}**. Stay in this language for all user-facing replies unless they switch first.

## TTS / STT
Pick one provider and stick to it. The OpenClaw `tts` and `stt` config blocks accept OpenAI, ElevenLabs, DeepGram, etc. Cheaper providers are fine for non-critical content (long narrations); use a higher-quality voice for short interactive replies.

(Add specific keys + voice IDs for your install here.)

## Web search
The `web_search` tool routes through whichever provider is wired in `tools.web.search.provider` (Perplexity, Tavily, Exa, Brave). The API key for the chosen provider must be in the bot's process env (typically loaded from `workspace/.env` by `setup-codex.sh`).
